---
import ChapterLayout from '../../../layouts/ChapterLayout.astro';
import { getDrakeChapter } from '../../../data/story/drakeChaptersData';
import { processDrakeContentHtml } from '../../../utils/drakeContentProcessor';

const chapter = getDrakeChapter('000-creator', 'southern-areas')!;

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;

const rawContentHtml = "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Part 22 kiddies, time to dive into a living nightmare!\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Beyond_Discord\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Beyond Discord</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Cornelia\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Cornelia</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Gulg_Volcano_Ring\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Gulg Volcano Ring</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Elven_Snowfields\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Elven Snowfields</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Melmond_Fens\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Melmond Fens</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Beyond_Discord\">Beyond Discord</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Beyond Discord\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_22?action=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Beyond Discord\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Before launching Scenario 000, let's cover a few things. First, the world is entirely wide-open, you can go anywhere you want in the southern regions and can go right for the first objective. This is a <i>bad</i> idea though, since the enemies in the objective gateway are quite high level, 90 in fact, and you're likely no higher than 50 after the main storyline, if even that. So I'm going to go around the world visiting other gateways and powering up the party before we get to the main mission. \n</p><p>000 lets you use a party of <i>any</i> five people you like, I will be using Zidane, Terra, Cloud, Lightning and Prishe. So, let's do it!\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>PLAYABLE CHARACTER - <b><span class=\"new\" title=\"Prishe/Dissidia (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUHJpc2hlL0Rpc3NpZGlhP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Prishe</span></b>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/3f/Prishe.png/revision/latest?cb=20110211225206\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Prishe\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/3f/Prishe.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/100?cb=20110211225206\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"324\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"Prishe.png\" data-image-key=\"Prishe.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Prishe is here, where's the grub? I've never played FF11, but as I understand it in her original game she's an immortal due to a crystal embedded in her chest that marks her as the mortal vessel for the day the twilight god Promathia will descend to the world, but the god was vanquished and Prishe made mortal. Naturally none of this comes up in D012. Prishe is a foul-mouthed, rowdy tomboy who loves a good brawl, and as seen in report flashbacks was one of the earlier fighters in the war with Shantotto. I quite like Prishe, she's a spunky lass and rather funny to listen to, especially once she hits Level 100 and you can unlock her hidden voice clips to randomly appear in battle. I won't spoil the fun, kiddies, level her up and find them for yourselves.\n</p><p>Prishe has a unique fighting style. She has eight Bravery combo attacks aside from the obligatory ranged ones. Each Bravery attack though can set one of the eight, including itself, as a follow-up attack, and much like an HP link, or more specifically Onion Knight's Bravery links, Prishe can then use two attacks in a row to pile up more damage. Combining certain skills like this together can create a Skillchain for even more damage. Prishe's attacks are Combo, a three-hit combo attack, Dragon Kick, a leg sweep that can be charged to crush guards and fire a projectile into the air, Howling Fist, a wind-up punch that crushes guard when charged, Should Tackle, a leaping shoulder charge, Spinning Attack, an aerial uppercut, Backhand Blow, a drop-down punch attack, Raging Fists, a five-hit combo, and One-inch Punch, a wind-elemental punch that crushes guards when charged. Phew! \n</p><p>Prishe's Skillchains do pretty massive damage, and she has quite a bit of tactical diversity with them too. As she levels up and learns them I'll be using the set-up I preferred in another file on this game - Combo-Combo, Howling Fist-Shoulder Tackle, Dragon Kick-Backhand Blow, One-Inch Punch-Howling Fist, Backhand Blow-One-Inch Punch, and Spinning Attack-Spinning Attack. You can use whichever set-ups you like. In her EX Mode, Prishe gets a movement speed boost and performs her second attacks twice in a row to do even more damage. Her EX Burst is pretty simple, a button command appears and then you quickly press them in sequence clockwise starting at that button.\n</p><p>I know I'm going in-depth on Prishe's Bravery game, and it's because that's her real strength - her HP attacks <i>suck</i>, oh how they suck! They aren't <i>bad</i> compared to each other, Auroral Uppercut is well, an uppercut, Banishga sends out a shockwave around her, Asuran Fists is a rapidfire punch barrage that reaches forward and into the air, and Nullifying Dropkick is a long-range homing dropkick. The problem with them is they all have massive start-up, making them ridiculously easy to avoid since the opponents in 000 are competent now, and forcing Prishe to rely on blocking and punishing, Assists, or Chases to deal HP damage.\n</p><p>However, in spite of her flaws Prishe is still one of my favorite D012 characters, her awesome Bravery game makes her a blast to play as, and I like using my Assists anyway so relying on them isn't too big a concern for me.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Also, screw honor now - go to the PP Catalog and buy out all the Exp calendar stuff! Suit up the party, if there are any new characters you're bringing along, put them in the back and let them get Exp without fighting. And now we're off!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cornelia\">Cornelia</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Cornelia\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_22?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Cornelia\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/e/ea/World_B_Cornelian_Plains.png/revision/latest?cb=20110505201041\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"World B Cornelian Plains\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/e/ea/World_B_Cornelian_Plains.png/revision/latest?cb=20110505201041\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"316\" height=\"196\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"World B Cornelian Plains.png\" data-image-key=\"World_B_Cornelian_Plains.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>As we begin, a voice calls out to us and asks us to come rescue it near Melmond, in the Chasm in the Rotting Land. We wake up on the beach near Cornelia, and a moogle is surprised to see us! Buy some Pebbles from it. The accessory line-up is up to you, I recommend a Hyper Ring with a Muscle Belt or Earring and whatever boosters you like, the Sunrise is not needed. Also as a note, at any time if you save and quit the storyline, when you re-launch it you can change your party freely.\n</p><p>Buy whatever limited items the moogle has for sale and go north and left, Final Fantasy fans will recognize this place as the ruins of the Chaos Shrine. The wiki has maps of this scenario so I'll provide them for you. Take the chest, chat with the moogle if you like, then return to Cornelia and enter the Gateway to Departure.\n</p><p>As we enter, spirits of fallen warriors call to us and offer their assistance, but warn they're not here to help you in your quest, they'll stay within the gateways and will attack if you approach them. Be warned - in all gateways, talking to your Assist will trigger a fight with their character, and they will always be level 100 with full equipment and strong accessories. Furthermore, flee or victory, they will vanish and you'll have to complete the gateway without an Assist. It's best to just avoid them unless they deliberately block your path, and I'll mention such circumstances.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235927\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"30,000 Gil\"><img alt=\"30,000 Gil\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203235927\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Rare Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Rare_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/e/ef/D012_Locked_Area.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209051329\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Complete &quot;Chasm in the Rotting Land&quot;\"><img alt=\"Complete &quot;Chasm in the Rotting Land&quot;\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Locked Area.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Locked_Area.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/e/ef/D012_Locked_Area.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209051329\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocooki